  "meaning": "Jubilee Year and Freedom",
  "description": "The number fifty represents freedom, release, and restoration. The fiftieth year was the Jubilee year (Lev 25:10), when slaves were freed, debts were canceled, and land was returned to its original owners. Pentecost (Shavuot) is celebrated on the fiftieth day after Passover, marking a deep connection between the old and new covenants: just as the Torah was given at Sinai, the Holy Spirit was poured out over the disciples on Pentecost (Acts 2). Fifty thus symbolizes both physical and spiritual liberation—jubilee in ancient Israel and the liberating power of the Spirit in the new covenant.",
